# Optional API keys. Eight of the ten sources work without any key — the Met,
# Art Institute of Chicago, Cleveland, Rijksmuseum, V&A, Japan Search and
# Wikidata all run unauthenticated. These two unlock the rest.
#
# Note: the server reads the process environment and does not load this file
# on its own. Either export the variables, run with `node --env-file=.env`, or
# set them in your MCP client's `env` block.

# Harvard Art Museums — request a free key:
# https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1Fe1H4nOhFkrLpaeBpLAnSrIMYvcAxnYWm0IU9a6IkFA/viewform
HARVARD_API_KEY=

# Smithsonian Open Access — free, instant, self-service from api.data.gov:
# https://api.data.gov/signup/
# Unlocks the National Museum of African Art, the National Museum of Asian Art
# and the National Museum of the American Indian. DEMO_KEY works for a quick
# try but is capped at 10 requests/hour, which is too low for real use.
SMITHSONIAN_API_KEY=

# Museum of New Zealand Te Papa Tongarewa — free registration:
# https://data.tepapa.govt.nz/docs/register.html
# Unlocks Taonga Māori and Pacific Cultures.
TEPAPA_API_KEY=
